# Absolute path prefixes for libraries provided by macOS itself.
#
# On macOS 11 and later most of these exist only inside the dyld shared cache and
# have no file on disk at all. References under these prefixes are pruned by the
# dependency walker with the highest precedence -- ahead of both the includelist
# and the excludelist.
#
# Why this is a separate file rather than excludelist entries: the includelist
# takes precedence over the excludelist, and patterns there such as
# `*/libz*.dylib` match `/usr/lib/libz.1.dylib`. An excludelist entry for
# `/usr/lib/*` would therefore be silently overridden, and the walker would try
# to bundle a file that does not exist. The same applies to `*/libintl*`,
# `*/libcrypto*`, `*/libssl*` and `*/libpcre*`. Only a rule that outranks both
# lists can distinguish the system copy of a library from vcpkg's.
#
# Matching is a plain prefix test, so each entry must be absolute and end in a
# slash -- otherwise `/usr/libfoo` would count as being under `/usr/lib`.
#
# Note what is deliberately absent: /usr/local/ and /opt/homebrew/ are Homebrew,
# not the operating system, and libraries found there have to be bundled.
/usr/lib/
/System/
/Library/Apple/
